# ==== testbench deck (exact input given to ngspice) ====
| * tb_pnp_mismatch.spice -- sky130 substrate-PNP local-mismatch Monte Carlo (issue #31)
| *
| * Device-level offset-budget input: sigma of dVBE across a matched PNP pair,
| * the term the untrimmed-accuracy budget for the error amplifier (#9) hangs
| * on. This is the sky130 counterpart of gf180-bandgap's
| * sim/device-pnp-mismatch/ and is deliberately NOT run through
| * sim/bin/corner-run.py: that runner drives one deterministic .op per PVT
| * point and has no notion of resampling a deck N times, which is exactly what
| * a local-mismatch claim needs. Driven instead by
| * sim/pnp-mismatch/run_pnp_mismatch.py.
| *
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * sky130 mismatch mechanism (verified against the pinned PDK, not assumed)
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * gf180mcu's convention (sw_stat_mismatch gating mis_is_pnp_* / mis_bf_pnp_*)
| * does NOT carry over. In sky130A the per-instance mismatch terms live inside
| * the device subcircuits in
| * libs.tech/combined/continuous/models_bjt.spice:
| *
| *   .subckt sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68 c b e mult=1
| *   .param mm_bf = {sw_mm_sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68_bf
| *                   * mismatch_factor * MC_MM_SWITCH * AGAUSS(0,1.0,1)/sqrt(mult)}
| *          mm_is = {sw_mm_sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68_is
| *                   * mismatch_factor * MC_MM_SWITCH * AGAUSS(0,1.0,1)/sqrt(mult)}
| *   ... is = '1.5075e-018*dkispp / sw_func_rdp*(1+mm_is)'
| *       bf = '19.35*dkbfpp*sw_nw_rs_mult**0.75*(1+mm_bf)'
| *       ise = '9.4936e-017*(1-mm_bf)'   vaf = '152.06 / sw_nw_rs_mult*(1-mm_bf)'
| *       xti = {1.1*(1+mm_is)}
| *
| * The sigmas themselves are in continuous/models_global.spice:
| *   sw_mm_sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68_is = 1.662e-02   (1.662 % on Is)
| *   sw_mm_sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68_bf = 5.537e-02   (5.537 % on Bf)
| * The W3p40L3p40 (large) subcircuit reuses the same two coefficients scaled by
| * 0.13 (is) and 0.45 (bf) -- the area-matching benefit of the 25x larger
| * emitter, already in the PDK model.
| *
| * The gate is MC_MM_SWITCH, and it is *not* settable from the deck: every
| * plain corner section of libs.tech/combined/sky130.lib.spice sets
| * `.param MC_MM_SWITCH=0`, and only the `*_mm` sections (tt_mm, ss_mm, ...)
| * set it to 1. The section name is therefore the switch. The run script
| * selects `tt_mm` for the mismatch points and `tt` for the control point
| * (which must return sigma == 0 exactly -- the falsification check against a
| * silently no-op mismatch setup).
| *
| * MC_PR_SWITCH (global process Monte Carlo, the `mc` section) stays 0: this
| * record is local mismatch only, see the process-axis note below.
| *
| * AGAUSS() is evaluated per subcircuit *instance*, so two instantiations of
| * the same subcircuit already draw independently -- no per-device parameter
| * plumbing is needed. ngspice re-draws on `reset`, which is what makes the
| * control loop below a genuine Monte Carlo; `setseed` makes it reproducible.
| *
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * Topology
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * Every DUT is diode-connected the way a bandgap core uses a sky130 substrate
| * PNP: collector (the p-substrate) and base (the nwell) grounded, emitter
| * driven by an ideal current source, so VEB = v(emitter). Subcircuit pin
| * order is (c b e), hence `X<name> 0 0 <emitter-node>`.
| *
| * NOTE, and read this before comparing absolute volts against
| * sim/pnp-characterization: that experiment's xschem netlist
| * (`XQS0 E_small_100n 0 0 sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68`) lands the driven
| * node on pin 1 = `c`, i.e. it biases the collector with the emitter grounded,
| * which measures the base-collector junction rather than the emitter-base one.
| * Reproduced exactly at tt/27 C/1 uA: collector-driven gives 0.545166 V
| * (matching that record's `veb_small_1u = 0.545166 V`), emitter-driven gives
| * 0.742539 V. This testbench uses the emitter-driven connection because that
| * is the connection a bandgap core actually has. See the record for the full
| * note; correcting sim/pnp-characterization is out of scope for issue #31.
| *
| * Two pairs, each at two bias currents (1 uA and 10 uA -- both are rungs of
| * sim/pnp-characterization's 100 nA..100 uA half-decade ladder and they
| * bracket the 2/5/20 uA per-branch range sim/mos-matching-characterization
| * uses for the < 50 uA total Iq budget; they are also the two biases
| * gf180-bandgap's mismatch record used, so the two repos compare directly):
| *   (a) identical pair: two W0p68L0p68 devices at equal emitter current --
| *       the pair offset any amplifier input or mirror built from this unit
| *       device sees.
| *   (b) area-ratioed pair: W0p68L0p68 / W3p40L3p40 at equal emitter current --
| *       the PTAT pair itself, so sigma(dVBE) here is directly comparable to
| *       the dVBE *signal* the same legs produce (reported as the sample mean).
| *
| * No supply rail exists in this deck: every DUT is referred to its own
| * emitter node and biased by an ideal current source. The +/-10 % supply axis
| * of the CLAUDE.md PVT matrix has nothing to sweep -- stated in the record as
| * the explicit subset justification (same justification
| * sim/pnp-characterization already records).
| *
| * Process axis: nominal only (`tt_mm`), deliberately not stacked on
| * tt/ss/ff/sf/fs. Local mismatch is intra-die variation; running it on top of
| * every global corner would double-count the global spread
| * sim/pnp-characterization's 15-point matrix already records. Also stated
| * inline in the record (this deck does not go through corner-run.py, so there
| * is no --subset-reason flag to carry it).
| *
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| * Inputs supplied by the run script (this deck is not standalone)
| * ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
| *   corner.spice  -- generated: `.lib <sky130.lib.spice> <section>` + `.temp`
| *   $mc_seed      -- ngspice variable, set from the generated .spiceinit
| *   $mc_runs      -- ngspice variable, set from the generated .spiceinit
| * The defaults below apply only if the deck is driven by hand.
| 
| .include corner.spice
| 
| * ---- identical pair: W0p68L0p68 x2, 1 uA ----
| Ia1a 0 ea1a 1u
| XA1a 0 0 ea1a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68
| Ia1b 0 ea1b 1u
| XA1b 0 0 ea1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68
| 
| * ---- identical pair: W0p68L0p68 x2, 10 uA ----
| Ia10a 0 ea10a 10u
| XA10a 0 0 ea10a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68
| Ia10b 0 ea10b 10u
| XA10b 0 0 ea10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68
| 
| * ---- area-ratioed pair: W0p68L0p68 / W3p40L3p40, 1 uA ----
| Ir1a 0 er1a 1u
| XR1a 0 0 er1a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68
| Ir1b 0 er1b 1u
| XR1b 0 0 er1b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| 
| * ---- area-ratioed pair: W0p68L0p68 / W3p40L3p40, 10 uA ----
| Ir10a 0 er10a 10u
| XR10a 0 0 er10a sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W0p68L0p68
| Ir10b 0 er10b 10u
| XR10b 0 0 er10b sky130_fd_pr__pnp_05v5_W3p40L3p40
| 
| .control
| if $?mc_seed
|   setseed $mc_seed
| else
|   setseed 20260731
| end
| if $?mc_runs
|   let nruns = $mc_runs
| else
|   let nruns = 300
| end
| set width  = 512
| set height = 100000
| let run = 0
| dowhile run < nruns
|   reset
|   op
|   let da1   = v(ea1a)  - v(ea1b)
|   let da10  = v(ea10a) - v(ea10b)
|   let dr1   = v(er1a)  - v(er1b)
|   let dr10  = v(er10a) - v(er10b)
|   let vr1a  = v(er1a)
|   let vr1b  = v(er1b)
|   let vr10a = v(er10a)
|   let vr10b = v(er10b)
|   print da1 da10 dr1 dr10 vr1a vr1b vr10a vr10b
|   let run = run + 1
| end
| quit
| .endc
| 
| .end

